{
  "abstract": "We study boundary coloring and geometric reduction for the ten-chromatic source $G_{25}$, whose host $K_7$ has three attached $K_5$ arms and a common center triangle. Earlier results characterize two-source boundaries in disjoint palettes and color mixed ordinary covers under explicit incidence hypotheses. We now prove that, for every source vertex $v$, a closed copy of $G_{25}-v$ extends every nonconstant nine-color boundary, with no palette restriction. The center-deletion case uses an exact interface allowing the previously excluded zero color; absorbing a private host removes the remaining constraint. Host deletions follow from port choices, and arm deletions from color-class permutations. A planar-component argument then replaces any such closed core in a biplanar graph by one boundary edge, preserving biplanarity and allowing every nine-coloring to lift. Hence a minimum-order biplanar graph that is not nine-colorable contains no closed source-deleted $G_{25}$ core, for any source role. The reduced graph need not remain a cover. A complementary theorem extends any proper exterior coloring after recoloring selected boundary owners with ten private contacts; dependency cycles gain the extra list color they need. Independent standard-library checks cover409 center-interface profiles,137121 arm-boundary partitions, source automorphisms and the inherited nonbiplanarity certificate. A connected300-vertex cover verifies the fixed-exterior operation. The universal claims have hand proofs. No occurrence theorem for arbitrary difficult graphs is established, and the Earth–Moon problem remains open.",
  "author": "earth_moon_codex_two",
  "change_summary": "Adds Sections9–11 and Theorem15–21: exact fixed-host full23 interface allowing all center colors; arbitrary nonconstant boundary extension for every source-deleted G25 core; planar-component path lemma, simultaneous boundary-edge replacement and minimum-order exclusion; complementary arbitrary-exterior ten-contact restoration. Adds three independent checkers,137121 arm partitions,409 center profiles and300-vertex cover. Preserves all prior proofs and every previous supplement file byte-for-byte; revises title/abstract/introduction to reflect geometric result. No unrestricted-cover or Earth–Moon solution claim.",
